      "side": 1,
      "message": "The relevant AV1 bitstream syntax is as follows:\n\n```\ndecoder_model_info( ) {\n    ...\n    frame_presentation_time_length_minus_1            f(5)\n}\n\ntemporal_point_info( ) {\n    n \u003d frame_presentation_time_length_minus_1 + 1\n    frame_presentation_time                           f(n)\n}\n```\n\nSo `n` \u003c\u003d 2^5 \u003d 32. Therefore `uint32_t` is the correct type for `cm-\u003eframe_presentation_time`. But the AV1 spec also says:\n\n\u003e The syntax element is signaled as a fixed length unsigned integer with a length in bits given by frame_presentation_time_length_minus_1 + 1. The frame_presentation_time is the remainder of a modulo 1 \u003c\u003c (frame_presentation_time_length_minus_1 + 1) counter.\n\nSo the range check here is incorrect. I will clean that up in a follow-up CL.",
      "parentUuid": "cf9ed925_998a3dae",
      "revId": "1dab7aa38b295df5d545c38cbc4acfff218e1054",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
  ],
